{title: 175 - Now the Green Blade Rises}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #175 • NOEL NOUVELET • 10.10.11.11}
{lyricist: John M. C. Crum}
{composer: French carol}
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 175}
{meta: tune NOEL NOUVELET}
{meta: meter 10.10.11.11}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Fm]Now the [Bb]green blade [Cm]rises [Bb/F]from the [Fm]buried grain,
[Fm]What that in dark [Bb7]earth many days [Cm]has lain;
[Fm/C]Love [Bb/F]lives again, [Fm]that with the dead has [Cm]been;
[Cm/G]Love is [Fm]come again like wheat arising [Cm]green.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Fm]In the [Bb]grave they [Cm]laid [Bb/F]Him, love by [Fm]hatred slain,
[Fm]Thinking that He [Bb7]would never wake [Cm]again,
[Fm/C]Laid [Bb/F]in the earth [Fm]like grain that sleeps unseen;
[Cm/G]Love is [Fm]come again like wheat arising [Cm]green.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Fm]Forth He [Bb]came in [Cm]triumph, [Bb/F]like the risen [Fm]grain,
[Fm]He that for three [Bb7]days in the grave [Cm]had lain;
[Fm/C]Raised [Bb/F]from the dead, [Fm]my living Lord is seen;
[Cm/G]Love is [Fm]come again like wheat arising [Cm]green.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Fm]When our [Bb]hearts are [Cm]wintry, [Bb/F]grieving, or [Fm]in pain,
[Fm]Your touch can call [Bb7]us back to life [Cm]again,
[Fm/C]Field [Bb/F]of our hearts [Fm]that dead and bare have been;
[Cm/G]Love is [Fm]come again like wheat arising [Cm]green.
{end_of_verse}
